{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/354458-how-much-experience","id":354458,"title":"How much experience?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-29T22:08:27-08:00","id":354458,"title":"How much experience?","content":"A conversation on another thread got me thinking, in the different CWoD games that people run, what is the average experience award the you give/receive per game session? In most game I have played in it is usually 2 to 3 per session. But I have seen it range from 1 to 5 as an average. Most of the STs who only gave 1 experience were considered stingy. Even 1 to 2 as an average was grumbled about. I usually average 3 per session on games I run. So What do you think is average? I'm curious to know. Thanks for sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T23:02:43-08:00","id":354506,"title":"","content":"For my group, we tend to run around 2-4 for a normal session (rarely someone would get 5), and 3-6 for end of story.<br /> Sometimes there are/were XP incentives for downtime (between sessions) notes/journals or activities (usually 1, rarely 2 extra XP). I don't know if you would count that towards the answer to your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T05:45:23-08:00","id":354689,"title":"","content":"2-4, only use 1 or 5 for special situations (blue booking, big story endings)<br /> <br /> Basically 2 is my minimum... 1 for showing up and 1 for role-playing to the character's traits (which I enforce during the game).<br /> <br /> Then I add a point if something significant happened that -changes- the setting. Since Mage is difficult to use linear plot lines, anything that the player does to actually change the game world counts.<br /> <br /> Then, I add a point if something significant happened that -changes- the character. Growth comes in a lot of forms, and honestly this one is almost a gimme with any experienced roleplayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T12:33:46-08:00","id":355971,"title":"","content":"If I ever give anyone just 1XP, it's cause they didn't do a damn thing all game and I'm sending a message--in the 16 years or so that I've been running cWoD games, I have given a single XP, perhaps, twice. Maybe three times.<br /> <br /> 2 XP is what I give for a particularly short game, or a game in which the players (or a given player, who then receives the 2 xp) just do housekeeping. This happens typically when I get far into a chronicle, and the players have acquired large holdings that require periodic management. It also happens when Mage players spend two hours designing (i.e., negotiating with me over) the functioning of wonder they want to make, and then making them.<br /> <br /> 3 XP is norm; 1 for showing up; 1 for engaging in the narrative; 1 for good faith role-playing. From here I can creep up to 4 or even 5. This is because I'll award another 1 for particularly excellent role-playing (this is not a moving target--I am fully prepared to award everyone the extra point, every single session, if they happen to bring it every single session); and another 1 for miscellaneous extraordinary performance--i.e., doing some really <i>really </i>cool; taking a serious risk (that is not unreasonable for that given character--so people can't just take arbitrary risks to try to get the extra point); or sometimes, just to punctuate the importance of something that happened in the game, so of like, &quot;alright folks, this was a fairly important and enriching thing that just happened, and you're all a little more badass for it...&quot;<br /> <br /> For end of game, I typically try to do at least 1 XP for every 1.5 sessions played; and then maybe a little gravy (2-3) in addition to that for a particularly harrowing or well-played arc overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}